# What the library needs at run time, exact pins rather than `>=` floors.
# src/requirements.txt is compiled from this file with hashes and installed
# with --require-hashes and wheels only by the `grade` job in
# .github/workflows/reusable-coderabbit-gate.yml, into the interpreter
# actions/setup-python gives it, before pin_only.py runs in a consumer's CI.
# Regenerate it with the command in its header, never by hand; Renovate's
# pip-compile manager bumps a pin here and replays that command.
#
# pyyaml reads a consumer's .github/pin-only.yml. The runner's own python3
# carries it as python3-yaml, but that interpreter is whatever Python the
# runner image ships, not the one this library is written and linted for.
pyyaml==6.0.3
